{"text":"Multi-negative training is a well-supported SASRec experiment. [gSASRec’s IJCAI 2024 extended abstract](https://www.ijcai.org/proceedings/2024/0939.pdf) combines multiple negatives with generalized BCE to reduce sampling-induced overconfidence; authors recommend 128–256 negatives and calibration parameter t=0.75, while acknowledging increased computation and memory. This supports testing negative count and objective jointly; it does not establish that ordinary multi-negative BCE or sampled softmax will improve this Amazon benchmark. [RecSys 2025’s sampled-softmax implementation](https://github.com/NonameUntitled/logq/) provides uniform, in-batch, and mixed sampling baselines plus revised LogQ correction—useful references when implementing nonuniform sampling.

Hardest-only mining has substantial caveats. [R²NS, WWW 2026](https://renzhaochun.github.io/assets/pdf/WWW_2026_Camera_Ready.pdf), reports that introducing difficult negatives too early can underperform uniform sampling. Its approach uses uniform warm-up, efficient approximate global retrieval, and progressively harder stochastic selection. Sampling among several high-scoring candidates reduces dependence on a single potentially false negative; an unobserved item is not necessarily disliked. Separately, a [2024 sequential-recommendation study](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.17276) finds sampling trade-offs vary across datasets and popularity bands, cautioning against assuming popularity or adaptive sampling universally wins.

Practical inference: first compare single-negative BCE against modest multi-negative sampled softmax and gBCE; then test a warm-started random/hard mixture. Exclude padding, target collisions, and observed training positives; treat remaining false negatives as uncertain rather than identifiable from scores alone. Start with 16–64 negatives as a budget-conscious experimental choice, escalating only if useful. Electronics’ supplied 14.95% outranking diagnostic motivates this ablation but cannot predict gains. Select exclusively by the pinned four-category macro validation HR@10, tracking GPU cost and category regressions."}
